        <groundspeak:log id="650079797">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-11-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3854161">Stonagal</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP560 - Hilliard

Not an easy one to get to, but the ditch was just dry enough not to cause problems. Someone had dug up the bottom of the sign, but the cap was further away than that so I'm not sure what it was for.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="617498575">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-11T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="2500583">Count Smiley</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP560 Hilliard

Mr. C decided to tackle this one directly through the water filled ditches while I took the dryer and more sensible route to the cap.  I returned to the vehicle with just some damp cuffs where as he returned like a giant sponge that had sucked all the moisture for the prairies.  There was no way that this potential storm cloud of a person was going to rain inside my new vehicle so I was able to fasten him securely to the roof racks for the remainder of the trip.   After all, that's what the roof racks were for, right?  A canoe or a Canoehead!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="617444744">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-11T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="228846">Mr. CanoeHead</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP560 Hilliard

The ditch was full of water and the vegetation thoroughly drenched but I attempted the ditch crossing ... it's a Canoehead pride thing ... blah, blah, no water shall deter me, blah, blah.   Got the cap and proudly returned to the vehicle only to be advised that my current state of saturation was not acceptable for in-vehicle transportation and that for the remainder of the trip I would need to join the canoe on the roof racks.   It was a cold, windy, bug splattered journey for me from there.   TFTCap&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
